{#
  Generic block renderer: walks a page's blocks[] and renders each by its
  `layout` discriminator (README §6).

  Every column layout resolves to the same container with a layout-suffixed
  class, and site/assets/css/style.css sizes the grid — so there is one rule
  here, not one branch per layout.

  `section_class` carries the section-level modifier classes the previous site
  put on each block: content-block-blue, content-block-cards,
  content-block-border-top and friends. The import dropped them, so pages that
  should have been blue sections with white text rendered white-on-white —
  /partnerships/ was six sections of it. The CSS for all of them was already
  ported; only the class was missing.

  twoimage-20 is the one layout whose inner container is not named after its
  layout; its own outer classes live in section_class, like everything else.
  raw:* is emitted verbatim, with no container and no section wrapper — used by
  the hand-built homepage and team sections, and by raw:cta, which renders the
  shared CTA component instead of the block's own HTML.

  block() only ever sees column layouts: the loop below dispatches raw:cta and
  every other raw:* before calling it, so the macro carried a raw: arm that
  could not run.
#}
{% macro block(b) %}
{%- if b.layout == "twoimage-20" -%}
<div class="content-block-container container content-block-container-twoimage content-block-container-with-image-left">{{ b.html | injectContactForm | safe }}</div>
{%- else -%}
<div class="content-block-container container content-block-container-{{ b.layout }}">{{ b.html | injectContactForm | safe }}</div>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{% for b in blocks %}
{%- if b.layout == "raw:cta" -%}
{% include "cta.njk" %}
{%- elif b.layout.startsWith("raw:") or b.html.trim().startsWith("<section") -%}
{#- Six blocks across five pages came out of the import with their whole
    <section> already in the html while still carrying a column `layout`.
    Wrapping those again nested a second .content-block inside the first, which
    doubled the 3em section padding and, for the sidebar layout, squeezed the
    inner grid into the outer grid's first column. They are emitted as-is. -#}
{{ b.html | injectContactForm | safe }}
{%- else -%}
<section class="content-block{% if b.section_class %} {{ b.section_class }}{% endif %}">{{ block(b) }}</section>
{%- endif -%}
{% endfor %}
